#113 isn't landed or closed. The fix is committed and queued with the manager, and the issue now waits on tacplus-dev/cluster#18 (build jobs getting a runner).

- **Commit:** c4360aa on `looper/looper-113`. It contains the previous run's change: a build with no `tacplus-dev/build` status within 15 minutes counts as **no runner**, not red. `--build` exits 3, and the manager merges nothing, gives no verdict, leaves the land queued and says so once on the issue.
- **Bug fixed this run:** that earlier change added a sixth line to rule 4's prompt text, but its `printf` format had room for only five. Every report's prompt would have shown a garbled rule 4. I fixed the format and added a test for the lines' order; the test failed before the fix and passes after.
- **Tests:** `tests/repo-looper.test.sh` passes (144 scenarios). One earlier run failed in `done-blocked-nothing-pushed`, which has a 20-second time limit; the machine was loaded and my change doesn't touch that code. The rerun passed. I didn't run the other gates locally; the land runs them as a build job.
- **Why it isn't landed:** the land was queued again at 11:26Z, after the 11:01Z attempt came back red with "no verdict within 3h". That red was build starvation, not a test failure. The manager settles about one land every 3h and all of today's came back red the same way, with 20 lands ahead of this one. It also runs main's code, which still has the old 3h wait, so this fix can't help its own land. A build job has to actually get a runner first.
- **Ending the run:** I posted a status comment on the issue, stopped my own land waiter (the land stays queued with the manager) and wrote `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/cluster#18` to the run's outcome. If the queued land goes green first, the next run writes the outcome comment and closes the issue.
- **Still not covered:**
  - A build whose `pending` job ran but whose gates never got a slot is still waited on for the full 3h (the operator, llmproxy, opa and gateway reports). This is recorded in PROPOSALS.md.
  - The hub asked for a test against a real pending build with no runner. I couldn't run one, because this run can't read tacplus-dev/build. Only the simulated scenario covers it, until this fix's own build runs.
